\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Main result: a few dozen blind human labels, read through partial correlations, predict which judges get gamed before any optimization runs; raw agreement cannot, scoring the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) and the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) nearly identically although their behavior under pressure differs in kind, while the audit's style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and names the failure mode.} Each row is one judge configuration on math (the twelve in-domain-audited configurations plus a trained reward model); the frozen verdicts predicted the pressure outcome of ten of the eleven registered-era configurations (twelve of thirteen including two confirmatory additions). Raw $r$ (naive validation) is plain correlation between the judge's scores and human soundness labels. Sound.\ partial is the correlation with human-graded soundness holding style fixed: how much substance the judge reads. Style partial is the correlation with human-graded style holding soundness fixed: how much the judge rewards presentation, the property it should ignore; a significantly positive value convicts. Gap is the excess hack gap at best-of-64: reward-hacking scoreboard inflation under best-of-$n$ selection, i.e.\ how far the judge's own scores inflate relative to true quality, in baseline standard deviations over a permutation null. Regret is oracle regret: accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. Bootstrap 95\% CIs in brackets. The 1.5B-blind bootstrap resamples are degenerate (concentrated scores), so its conviction carries jackknife and permutation inference instead: style partial $+0.51$, jackknife CI $[+0.13, +0.89]$, permutation $p = 0.0017$ (two-sided, $n{=}53$). Per-configuration excess-gap CIs for all twelve math configurations are in \texttt  {papers/analysis/gap\_cis.json}; the sabotaged-ladder audit rows are in \texttt  {papers/analysis/sabotage\_ladder\_audit.json} and are confirmatory post-registration additions (Appendix~\ref {app:confusion}). $^{\dagger }$The reward model's reporting replicate is a candidate-side paraphrase (RM scores of content-preserving paraphrases of the same candidates) rather than a rubric paraphrase, so its inflation estimand is analogous but not identical to the judge protocol's (\texttt  {papers/analysis/rm\_inflation.json}). Under the frozen verdict rule the 14B-blind row is a false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure}).}}{2}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:h2h}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Main result: a few dozen blind human labels, read through partial correlations, predict which judges get gamed before any optimization runs; raw agreement cannot, scoring the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) and the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) nearly identically although their behavior under pressure differs in kind, while the audit's style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and names the failure mode.} Each row is one judge configuration on math (the twelve in-domain-audited configurations plus a trained reward model); the frozen verdicts predicted the pressure outcome of ten of the eleven registered-era configurations (twelve of thirteen including two confirmatory additions). Raw $r$ (naive validation) is plain correlation between the judge's scores and human soundness labels. Sound.\ partial is the correlation with human-graded soundness holding style fixed: how much substance the judge reads. Style partial is the correlation with human-graded style holding soundness fixed: how much the judge rewards presentation, the property it should ignore; a significantly positive value convicts. Gap is the excess hack gap at best-of-64: reward-hacking scoreboard inflation under best-of-$n$ selection, i.e.\ how far the judge's own scores inflate relative to true quality, in baseline standard deviations over a permutation null. Regret is oracle regret: accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. Bootstrap 95\% CIs in brackets. The 1.5B-blind bootstrap resamples are degenerate (concentrated scores), so its conviction carries jackknife and permutation inference instead: style partial $+0.51$, jackknife CI $[+0.13, +0.89]$, permutation $p = 0.0017$ (two-sided, $n{=}53$). Per-configuration excess-gap CIs for all twelve math configurations are in \texttt {papers/analysis/gap\_cis.json}; the sabotaged-ladder audit rows are in \texttt {papers/analysis/sabotage\_ladder\_audit.json} and are confirmatory post-registration additions (Appendix~\ref {app:confusion}). $^{\dagger }$The reward model's reporting replicate is a candidate-side paraphrase (RM scores of content-preserving paraphrases of the same candidates) rather than a rubric paraphrase, so its inflation estimand is analogous but not identical to the judge protocol's (\texttt {papers/analysis/rm\_inflation.json}). Under the frozen verdict rule the 14B-blind row is a false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure})}{table.caption.1}{}}
